WEBVTT

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.930
DISASTERS CAUSED
BY SUPER USELESS ABILITIES

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.600
"The Super Useless Abilities" submitted to
<i>Weekly Jump</i> by its readers are featured.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.480
-What happened, Kusuo?
-Are you all right?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>I don't know.</i>
<i>Something's wrong with my limiter.</i>

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.320
He looks tired.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.440
<i>But it doesn't seem</i>
<i>to be completely broken.</i>

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.570
<i>It's different from what I feel</i>
<i>when I remove it.</i>

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.030
<i>I could fix it</i>
<i>with my restoration ability,</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.240
<i>but it can be restored to the default.</i>

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.700
Let me see that, Kusuo.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.660
<i>No, don't get close to me.</i>
<i>It might not be safe.</i>

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.370
What're you doing, honey?

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.290
I can't touch you.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.710
-There's an invisible wall around you.
<i>-What?</i>

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.080
Super Useless Ability 1: Invisible shield
covering a 50-cm radius for a day

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.670
<i>I see. Is that because I said</i>
<i>not to get close to me?</i>

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.250
<i>No object can go through.</i>

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.210
Hey, don't squish me...

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.050
<i>Oh, how useful.</i>
<i>I mean, such a useless ability.</i>

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.510
<i>And this cannot be deactivated.</i>

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.430
Stop mulling!

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.800
<i>Oh. Well, what should I do?</i>

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.810
<i>What's so funny, Mom?</i>

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.230
<i>No, it's a psychic ability again.</i>

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.140
Super Useless Ability 2:
Changing other's sense of humor

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.020
Honey, your clothes are so funny!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.610
<i>Is that what she's laughing at?</i>

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.320
Darling, your hair!

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.280
<i>Dad, too? Oh, shit.</i>
<i>This is out of control.</i>

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.320
I see. You have unknown psychic abilities.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.030
Oh, my goodness!

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.320
<i>It's more than that.</i>

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.990
<i>It activates by itself. So dangerous.</i>

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>And so annoying.</i>

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.620
<i>I can't even sit on the chair</i>
<i>because of this shield.</i>

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.120
What do we do?

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.710
Why don't we have some coffee
in an elegant manner and calm down.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.880
Super Useless Ability 3:
Making coffee bitter and ruining elegancy

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.670
Are you all right? Here's tea.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.090
Super Useless Ability 4:
Changing any drinks into soda

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:37.800
<i>Sorry, looks like it was me again.</i>

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.340
Damn! Do something!

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.050
<i>Now you know how serious the problem is.</i>

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.270
This isn't fair! Why is it always me?

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.600
<i>What goes around comes around.</i>

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.560
<i>A Matryoshka doll. How did it get here?</i>

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.060
<i>What? They keep coming out of my hand.</i>

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:50.980
Super Useless Ability 5:
Producing Matryoshka dolls from hands

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.440
<i>Gross! Isn't this a plagiarized idea</i>
<i>from </i>My Hero Academia?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.150
<i>Shoot, the shield keeps</i>
<i>Matryoshka dolls inside.</i>

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.070
<i>I don't want to drown in the dolls.</i>

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.700
<i>I must deactivate this shield.</i>

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.200
-Are you okay, Kusuo?
<i>-How could you laugh in this situation?</i>

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.000
<i>I broke the shield.</i>

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.420
What did you just shoot?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.790
<i>I don't know. It just came out.</i>

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.750
Super Useless Ability 6:
Producing beams from eyes

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.880
It passed right beside my face!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.960
<i>By the way, you were laughing</i>
<i>when I was in trouble.</i>

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.670
No, I was worried as hell.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.090
Oh, that's because
my sense of humor was controlled.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.180
<i>Oh, well. I'm getting irritated.</i>

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.550
What's this noise?

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.350
<i>Dad's collection of action figures</i>
<i>was just reduced to sand.</i>

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.060
What? You did it on purpose!
Spontaneously!

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>It discharged accidentally.</i>

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.850
-Liar!
<i>-Look.</i>

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:31.770
Super Useless Ability 7:
Degrading the collection

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.020
Have I done anything to him?

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.990
Jeez, why only me? It's better
than getting her involved, though.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.070
Honey, what are you doing?

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:39.990
Honey?

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:40.990
Super Useless Ability 8:
Infantilizing people's minds

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.200
Honey, you can't eat that!

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.290
Oh, sorry, sorry. Kusuo, soothe her!

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.120
<i>I have never used this kind of ability.</i>

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.080
<i>I'll give it a try. Get back to normal.</i>

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.040
-Did you make it?
<i>-Just our hair got swapped.</i>

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:52.960
What the hell...

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:53.880
Super Useless Ability 9:
Hairstyle swapping

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.420
<i>-Shit! One more time.</i>
-A large flock of crows!

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.340
Super Useless Ability 10:
Summoning a murder of crows.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.300
<i>Saiki kept trying to solve it.</i>

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.220
Super Useless Ability 11:
Seeing the age of skin

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.260
I'm fairly shocked!

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.180
Super Useless Ability 12:
Hiding Rated-Rs with lights or steam

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.260
I'm not R-rated! Okay to show!

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.220
Super Useless Ability 13:
Changing all voices to Hiroshi Kamiya's

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.140
VOICE CAST: HIROSHI KAMIYA

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.180
What a great voice. I don't need this now!

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.890
<i>His efforts were in vain.</i>

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.980
Enough! I will raise this girl!

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.360
<i>No matter how many times I try,</i>
<i>I just fail. What should I do?</i>

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.150
<i>I feel like I'm forced to pick up</i>
<i>psychic cards randomly.</i>

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.860
You mean, we can't get back to normal

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.990
until you pick an ability
that changes this situation?

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.820
<i>Mom has already returned to normal.</i>

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.280
Oh, you got me.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.620
What? Don't you realize
how worried about you I was?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.870
-Because I wanted you to care about me!
-Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.330
<i>There's no big difference in her case.</i>

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.790
Don't be silly.
You didn't have to do that.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.290
-I always care about you.
-Honey.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.210
Super Useless Ability 14:
Evaporating body water

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.050
Are you trying to kill me?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.470
No more! Your mother is herself again

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.340
<i>My limiter isn't fixed yet.</i>

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.680
Ask Kusuke for a replacement.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.060
<i>I don't want to owe him.</i>

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:51.270
<i>There should be one</i>
<i>that resolves everything. This!</i>

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.230
Super Useless Ability 15:
Getting something to hit Kaidou's shin

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.400
-Ouch!
-Are you okay?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.690
<i>No, the next one.</i>

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:56.650
Super Useless Ability 16: Turning men near
Teruhashi-san into unknown creatures

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.150
-I'm home.
-Welcome back, Kokomi!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.110
What? He's gone.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.570
<i>Not this one. This one on the other side.</i>

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.490
Super Useless Ability 17:
Creating something from nothing

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.950
<i>Great. I've got a new limiter.</i>

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.910
-Case solved!
-Wonderful.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:14.710
<i>Oh, well. I'm back to myself.</i>
<i>But I can no longer use those abilities.</i>

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.880
<i>Well, that's fine. They're all useless.</i>

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.300
<i>No, the last one wasn't useless.</i>

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.890
BUILD THE MOST POWERFUL DECK!

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.100
I've got nothing to do.
Wanna go eat ramen noodles?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.730
<i>I eat ramen when I get hungry.</i>

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.140
<i>Not when I have nothing to do.</i>

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.150
There's a little guy I have seen before.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:37.360
<i>You're his big friend.</i>

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.940
Master, I lost to Shigeo-kun again!

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.610
Idiot, let me see your deck of cards.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.700
Oh, come on, you have too many fires.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.620
What are you doing here, little man?

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.660
I... was just going to use the washroom.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:55.120
Seems like you are having
so much fun with kids, Master?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.210
<i>He saw everything!</i>

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.420
Hanging out with small kids
at a toy store at your age?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.210
Shut up! Stupid!

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.300
<i>You're a little brat, too,</i>
<i>since you couldn't just ignore him.</i>

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.130
What are you standing in a line for?

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.220
"Vallo-kyorie-a-brai-akira"?

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.180
"Bal-kyori-a-bre-akira"!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.680
It's <i>"Valkyrie Breaker,"</i> idiot!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.680
You are looking down on it,

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.690
but even adults enjoy
playing this intellectual game.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.150
It's a mental battle
that requires strategies and tactics.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.400
-It's a game of darkness.
<i>-What's good about darkness?</i>

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.570
Master, can you play with me?

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.990
I'll finally defeat you after losing
to you 67 times in a row today!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.620
<i>He has beaten him brutally.</i>

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.950
Anyways, don't think this one
is like other children's games!

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:35.410
It must be too hard to play, for an idiot
who can't even read <i>Valkyrie Breaker!</i>

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.750
Oh, is that so? You've said enough.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.670
-Why don't you play against us idiots?
<i>-What?</i>

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.050
-For real? Saiki, will you play, too?
<i>-I won't.</i>

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.680
-You'll be one of <i>Breakers</i> players, too!
<i>-I won't.</i>

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.350
Oh, I'm so happy that Saiki will join us!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:54.140
I've been bloodthirsty for battles
due to the absence of men with spirit.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.930
I said I'd play, too!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.400
-Come on! Let's play! I'll butter you!
<i>-Why will you make him greasy?</i>

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:00.980
Are you stupid?

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.110
You need a deck of cards first.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.820
We have cards here.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.610
These are mine!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.450
<i>First, explain to him how it's different</i>
<i>from normal playing cards.</i>

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.740
You need these expensive cards.
Go get them if you want to play!

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.450
What a drag...

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.870
<i>Okay, I'll pretend to go get cards</i>
<i>so I can go home.</i>

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.420
Wait, you don't need to go get any.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.960
-You can use these.
<i>-How efficient.</i>

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:26.510
Oh, don't worry! I don' t use them anyway.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.680
If you are serious about this,
you'd better have these to start at least.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.930
<i>How can I leave now?</i>

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:34.760
<i>Oh, well. If I get serious,</i>
<i>I will be the world champion.</i>

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.230
<i>But he hasn't stalked me much</i>
<i>since he got into this game.</i>

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.230
I was getting tired of playing this
due to lack of good opponents.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.730
<i>I don't want him to stop playing it.</i>

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.230
Hey, I've got one.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.860
I will build an original
and all-powerful deck of cards.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.950
<i>Where did you go?</i>

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.950
The store employee told me
that there are rare cards.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.540
That's right. Saiki,
open the package I just gave you.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.040
Ferocious Squirrel, Zebra Rider,
Dashing Koala, Jumping Rabbit...

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.960
-What did you get?
-I can't read it. A weird one.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.050
Golden Lion King Mike?

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.920
That's the most powerful card ever sold!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.470
Is it that good?

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:10.050
It's way better than good!

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.640
Master's spent 30,000 yen to get Mike.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.890
-But you got it at the first try! Wow!
<i>-Yeah...</i>

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.680
Great! I will get more!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.060
-I got the same one again!
-Again!

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.650
That's impossible...

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.320
<i>I checked all packages</i>
<i>with my second sight</i>

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.610
<i>and replaced all the rare cards</i>
<i>with Nendou's.</i>

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.990
<i>I need him to be into it.</i>

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.820
<i>To make him so, he needs to be</i>
<i>as good as Kaidou.</i>

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.790
<i>Then they will get into the game,</i>
<i>and I will grow apart from them.</i>

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.870
Even though you're equipped
with strong attack cards,

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.870
you can't win without
good magic and trap cards.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.630
You have to have a deck
of nicely balanced cards.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.090
-Oh, I've got a combination.
-Not fair!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.300
Wow, that's perfect!

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.590
Wow, your deck looks better than Master's,
on which he's spent over 100,000 yen.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.640
-Maybe I should quit.
<i>-I overdid it.</i>

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.140
You're so different from Master!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:00.930
Is Master the guy who gives us worthless
cards with a smug look on his face?

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.310
<i>Stop right there.</i>
<i>His life has already been reduced to zero.</i>

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:07.900
Bring it on, Nendou! I can teach you
that what cards you have isn't important!

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.860
-Sounds good to me.
-What? Are you going to have a battle?

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:15.370
<i>I won't forgive you. I'll make you regret</i>
<i>that you vandalized my sanctuary.</i>

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.200
Come and get me!

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.330
All right, I've got a pair.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.410
It's your turn.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.330
That's <i>Old Maid.</i>

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.500
<i>Next episode is Nendou vs. Kaidou.</i>
<i>Please stand by for the battle.</i>

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:30.960
THE DIE IS CAST! FIERCE CARD BATTLE

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:33.430
<i>The card battle continues.</i>

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.640
You're naive, little man.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:36.850
Look at this pair!

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.680
-I've got two of them.
-This is not <i>Memory!</i>

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.770
<i>Teaching Japanese</i>
<i>to monkeys must be easier.</i>

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:47.190
I will explain the rules
of <i>Valkyrie Breaker</i> to you again.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.900
First of all, there are mainly
three types of cards.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.690
It's game over
when your life reaches zero.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.280
-Did you get it?
-Yeah.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.200
<i>He didn't get anything at all.</i>

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.370
There are three monster groups:

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:59.030
Fire, Water and Ice.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.910
<i>Couldn't they think</i>
<i>of better-balanced groups?</i>

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.870
Any questions so far?

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.000
-No.
<i>-He is no longer listening.</i>

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.710
You can use monster cards as defense.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.460
-This is great!
-Understood?

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:09.540
<i>He is reading manga.</i>

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.590
-There's another rule...
-This manga...

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.420
-When someone is not listening...
-...is great!

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.380
-...you can stab him hard in the eyeballs!
-So funny.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.760
<i>Don't try this at home.</i>

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.140
Listen!

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.430
-What the hell?
-I'm explaining to you!

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:22.470
Stop it, Master!

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.180
You shouldn't hurt your friend.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.690
Stop bullying him!

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.190
Master, you told us,

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:29.770
<i>when we fought over cards...</i>

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:33.110
Stop it! If you're a <i>Breaker</i> player,
you should settle through a card battle.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.820
-You said so.
-Yeah, but it's nothing to do with...

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:38.740
-Let's fight together!
-Master is now our enemy!

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:39.820
I'm in!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:41.120
We're gonna beat Kaidou-san!

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.830
We definitely will!

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:43.910
-Kaidou-"san"?
<i>-Poor guy...</i>

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.920
<i>Now, kids joined Nendou, and...</i>

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.750
<i>the Nendou-vs-Kaidou-san battle has begun.</i>

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.300
<i>With 5,000 life points, no time limits,</i>
<i>the game begins.</i>

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.460
Let's Breaking!

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.840
<i>The phrase to begin is too tacky.</i>

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.340
<i>Damn, how could you take away</i>
<i>my obedient subordinates?</i>

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.810
<i>It's okay. I'll show you that a flock</i>
<i>of losers is no competition to me.</i>

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.260
My turn is over.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.390
<i>What's the card laying face</i><i>down?</i>

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.730
Doesn't matter. I'll just blow them up!
My turn!

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.150
I summon Ducktail Crocodile!

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.320
-Attack on Nendou's monster card!
<i>-Something popped up.</i>

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.780
-Nendou's monster card is Sly Monkey.
<i>-Popped up again.</i>

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.110
Which one's gonna win?

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.200
<i>Shouldn't we care more about the things</i>
<i>popping up from the cards?</i>

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.830
Oh, man, Ducktail Crocodile won!

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.040
<i>And it's rather gross.</i>

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.250
My turn isn't over yet.
A special effect: Coalition!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.540
I can summon the monster I defeated
as my own!

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:30.960
What?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.880
<i>Too many disturbing images.</i>

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.630
<i>Am I the only one</i>
<i>who can see those images?</i>

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.590
<i>-What kind of ability is this?</i>
-And the monster attacks!

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.550
I put a card facedown and my turn ends.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.050
He is too good.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.520
Isn't he ashamed to say "my turn"
at his age?

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.770
This is embarrassing to watch.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.020
He is tough-minded.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.270
<i>He sure was excited.</i>

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.360
-Let's make a counterattack!
-Yeah! It's my turn!

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.570
I summon Green Caterpillar.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:56.570
<i>Hey, not bugs.</i>

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.740
Also, a magic card
which was laid face down.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:02.070
With Equipment For Legendary Hero,
the power of Green Caterpillar is doubled.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.030
<i>Is it really doubled?</i>

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.120
Go!

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.120
<i>How is it gonna fight?</i>

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.460
Damn! I've lost my Ducktail Crocodile!

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.300
Is that what you expected to hear?

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:19.130
Take this! Phenomenal Self-Destruction!

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.090
<i>Hey, wait...</i>

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:24.430
<i>Gross.</i>

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.600
Oh, you boosted Green Caterpillar!

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.310
Is it that bad?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.890
It's the best timing.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.850
-It can't be...
-That's right! My turn!

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.360
Sacrificing the Sly Monkey,

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.730
I summon Golden Lion King Mike.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.110
There he comes!

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.320
Go, get him, Mike!
Direct Attack on Nendou!

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.830
<i>As I intended,</i>
<i>Kaidou-san will probably win.</i>

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.870
<i>But is it really okay?</i>

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.000
My turn is over.
You can surrender if you want!

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.500
-What should I do now?
-That's it! Use that card!

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:59.710
This is... Klein's Vase!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.300
It enables players to swap their cards.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.760
We're not done yet, Kaidou-san!

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.680
I summon Golden Lion King Mike
without sacrificing.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.520
No!

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:13.190
You're cheating! How could you have
Klein's Vase at such a great moment?

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:15.480
<i>I reordered the cards.</i>

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.730
<i>I was going to let Kaidou win,</i>
<i>but I changed my mind because it's gross.</i>

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.440
<i>I couldn't bear</i>
<i>if he played it on my desk.</i>

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:25.160
I still have a chance if I can draw
another Klein's Vase. Please!

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.120
FEROCIOUS SQUIRREL

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.040
<i>Kaidou-san, you lost.</i>

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:35.960
METORI SAIKO'S EQUATION OF VICTORY

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.420
Stop him!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.090
I've got it!

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:43.130
-He did it!
-Awesome!

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.550
<i>Oh, well. Hairo is so passionate,</i>
<i>as always.</i>

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:49.470
<i>How could he be so serious during recess</i>
<i>before the PE class?</i>

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.060
We'll play basketball in PE today.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.270
I used to play street basketball
in the US.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.520
<i>-Kaidou...</i>
-Here is a ball.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:59.230
<i>Are you an old guy who's playing</i>
<i>basketball for the first time in 80 years?</i>

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.190
<i>Go home.</i>

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:03.190
Do they use their faces
to dribble in the US?

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.240
Shut up! That's right! This is how
they play it in its birthplace!

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.370
-For real? That's awesome.
-Nendou-kun!

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:10.910
Are you confident about today's game?

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:14.500
I think so. People used to call me
"Nen-chan of basketball."

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.210
We'll play against each other.
Good luck to both of us!

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.210
<i>I will win you back today, Nendou-kun!</i>

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.300
All right, it's a five-on-five.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.210
RED TEAM

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.380
-Are you ready?
-We ended up being on the same team.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.840
Excuse me!

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.340
Nendou-kun and I
shouldn't be on the same team.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.800
We randomly chose the teammates.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:31.180
But we have Kuboyasu-kun, too!

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.100
BLUE TEAM

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.390
-It will be a one-sided game.
<i>-Can I thrash you?</i>

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.600
There are only four of them.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.690
Hey, what are you doing there? Get in!

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.270
-Saiko, line up!
-What?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.780
<i>He is not even in PE clothes.</i>

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:46.030
It's okay. You can just pretend
as if my team won, Mr. Low-Income.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.160
Get in line now!

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.240
It won't make any difference
if he joins or not.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.080
Right. He'd rather be a disadvantage
for us.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.450
I have no choice. Let's do a four-on-four
without Takahashi.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:57.420
Hold on! Leaving Takahashi out?

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.210
Are you saying I'm equal to him?

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.090
Don't be ridiculous!
This is an insult to me!

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.840
Pick the poor, passionate guy
or the poor idiot!

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:04.050
<i>-Is that what you care for the most?</i>
-Then, get in.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:07.470
-Wow, Saiko will participate in PE.
-This is the first time I've seen this.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:08.380
Dollar?

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.220
Are you ready to be humiliated?

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.310
If I didn't play,
your team could have a complete victory.

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:14.680
You'll see who gets humiliated.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.190
<i>We don't know how good he is</i>
<i>since he never participates in PE class,</i>

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:21.270
<i>but I don't think he can completely</i>
<i>close the power gap, either. It's a bluff!</i>

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.360
<i>We will win by a landslide so that</i>
<i>the teacher will shuffle the teams.</i>

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.570
Game begins!

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:27.820
Great, Nendou-kun!

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.240
Where are you aiming at?

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.910
Both money and balls gather around me.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.990
Now, let's play ball!

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.450
<i>Let us see you in action!</i>

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.920
Look at my beautiful dribbling technique!

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.880
So cocky.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.340
-What the hell is that move?
-Don't laugh at him.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.210
Please reconsider the teams!

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:48.930
<i>Watch out.</i>

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.430
-What?
-Was it funny?

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.640
You were laughing out loud.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.020
I would have laughed
if I was unintelligent like you.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.850
Your laughing face
could made me laugh even harder.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.230
-I'll kill you!
-Kuboyasu-kun! No, don't get heated!

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:05.650
I know! This is not a fight!
We settle this through basketball.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:06.610
3 MINUTES LATER

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:08.690
<i>-Kuboyasu-kun!</i>
<i>-I'd have won if it was a fight.</i>

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.610
FIVE FOULS AND KICKED OUT

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.070
No reserves, so it's a five-on-four now.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.030
<i>It's a huge disadvantage for us.</i>

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.870
<i>But we won't lose! I noticed something</i>
<i>from your play, Saiko-kun.</i>

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.920
<i>Your skill isn't as good</i>
<i>as it seems to be.</i>

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.670
<i>Kuboyasu-kun wouldn't have lost</i>
<i>if he could have stayed calm.</i>

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.500
<i>And there's Nendou-kun on our team.</i>

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:26.960
<i>And Kaidou-kun is on their team!</i>

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.670
<i>-We will not lose!</i>
-Nendou, pass me the ball!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.260
-I got it!
-Thanks.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.550
Nendou-kun! You can't pass the ball
to the opponent!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.930
Sorry, I thought I passed it
to my teammate.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:38.770
Yes, I am your teammate.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.730
-Oh, are you?
-He's not!

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.690
<i>Nendou-kun's weakness,</i>
<i>his stupidity, is targeted.</i>

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.520
<i>-We're driven into a corner!</i>
-Hairo! Here!

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.190
<i>We just have to do our best</i>
<i>with only three players.</i>

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.110
Good ball!

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.650
He stole my ball...

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:53.360
Cut it out!

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.910
You thought he was on your side?
It's Takahashi.

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:59.790
<i>-Are we going to lose to such a weak team?</i>
-I knew it from the beginning!

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:01.830
-Game is over!
<i>-Wrong.</i>

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.290
-I thought I made it!
<i>-This is not six-on-two but five-on-three.</i>

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:07.880
<i>I was just observing,</i>
<i>but bribery is out of question.</i>

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.880
-I'm going to score this time!
<i>-You can't. I applied an invisible shield.</i>

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:12.550
10 - 8
RED - BLUE

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:15.260
That's it! Red won against Blue
by a score of ten to eight.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.850
<i>Sorry, but I don't want another game.</i>

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.810
<i>The team won, but I feel like I lost.</i>

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.100
<i>Saiko-kun, you're amazing.</i>

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:25.690
<i>I hope to play with you again.</i>
<i>I wish he'd participate in PE more.</i>

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.530
<i>There's no such word as "defeat"</i>
<i>for the Saiko family.</i>

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.280
<i>Hairo, I will defeat you</i>
<i>in the next PE class!</i>

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.360
What happened to him?
He rarely does a workout.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:35.360
I have no idea.

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:41.000
HERO IN DISASTER

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.960
The Disastrous Life of Saiki K.,
serialized in <i>Weekly Jump</i>

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.000
since Vol. 24 of 2012,
marked its 5th anniversary!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.380
<i>The Disastrous Life of Saiki K.</i> marked
its 5th anniversary?

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.500
Congratulations!
What a great accomplishment!

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.380
-Is it that good?
-Don't get excited for only five years.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.680
-Who is that?
-We marked the 10th anniversary.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.590
OUR HERO STUDIES

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:57.430
It's been since Vol. 24 of 2007.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:58.930
Catch me if you can!

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:00.140
<i>Your series have already ended.</i>

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.310
I can give you my praise at least,

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.650
but it'll be difficult
to continue the series as is.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.900
Well, learning our "Hero's Studies"
will help you though.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.230
-Listen well.
<i>-Are they still gonna talk about that?</i>

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.730
Don't be satisfied with only five years.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.650
It's even shorter than years
to attend elementary school.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.990
Who the hell are you?

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.110
Watch your mouth!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.490
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:20.910
That's why I asked you who you are.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:22.410
Stop it, Nendou! You're so rude!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.750
What? Do you know them, little man?

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:28.170
Yeah, for sure. That bizarre outfit,
the sword on his back...

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:30.550
Could it be that you're Mr. Ken Haganeno?

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.170
Did you notice?

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.840
Wow, he is the real one!

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.050
-Habanero?
-Haganeno!

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.050
Haven't you seen him on the news on TV?

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.560
He is the most famous high school teacher!

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:43.060
Come to think about it, maybe I have.

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.270
So, you finally know who we are.

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.690
-And who is this guy?
<i>-No idea.</i>

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.310
Mr. Haganeno,
can I shake your hand, please?

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.230
HANDSHAKE FOR 1,080 YEN

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:51.230
It's 1,080 yen for shaking his hand.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.820
-Will you charge me?
-Of course.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.610
-By the way, who are you guys?
-Me?

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.320
I'm Nozomi Hinoki. I'm his manager.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.530
He is Masayuki.
He's handling the guillotine.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:01.450
Handling what?

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:04.950
What is such a famous teacher
doing here in front of our school?

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.460
Don't you know?

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:10.710
So, Mr. Haganeno will give us
a special lecture today.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.130
Hi. Whether you know me or not,

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.470
I'm the legendary hero and teacher
Ken Haganeno.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.630
<i>-5th anniversary, huh?</i>
-Wow, is he real?

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.720
He's been talked about in the news a lot.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:23.390
It's an honor that such a famous teacher
will give us a lecture.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.730
<i>-Don't bring a prowler in.</i>
-Let's talk about the fees.

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.730
All right, let me tell you something.

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:29.480
-You guys are trash.
<i>-No introduction?</i>

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.610
You guys are totally hopeless.
A total waste.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.360
It's a miracle that this series lasted
for five years.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.190
-Five years? What's that about?
-There's one thing you lack.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.110
What we lack?

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:39.200
Courage, kindness and strength.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.160
<i>He said three things.</i>

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:42.620
You lack these. For example...

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:45.830
The little man, it's obvious that you're
chickenhearted and have no courage.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.120
-Me?
<i>-He has more courage than you.</i>

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.750
You, the empty-headed gorilla,
living without a concept of kindness.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.130
<i>He's kinder than you.</i>

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.590
You, the plain and weak four-eyes, who can
be robbed even by middle-school kids.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:56.880
<i>Not weaker than you.</i>

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.340
See? What a disappointment.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:18:59.380
<i>You are.</i>

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:02.390
But you will be fine, since I, the one
who possess those three, am here.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:04.390
I'll be the main character of this anime,

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.720
and I'll help you all
to become great heroes.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.140
<i>He said something ridiculous</i>
<i>without hesitation.</i>

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.140
-Main character?
-I don't know...

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.610
-Mr. Haganeno is still talking!
-Who is that guy?

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.110
Let's listen to him anyways.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.400
<i>Don't wear our uniforms.</i>

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.490
They're transfer students.
Be nice to them.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:18.400
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.660
<i>They're trying to take over this anime.</i>
<i>It's not funny.</i>

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:22.740
HERO'S STUDIES

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.200
All right, let the class begin.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.660
-Hustle-and-bustle hero quiz!
<i>-Stop it.</i>

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.160
Okay, the first person is...

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.460
-You!
-Me?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:32.670
Your face irritates me,
so you are disqualified!

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.540
<i>Stop it. Don't hurt him without cause.</i>

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:39.050
<i>Haven't you learned that no one finds</i>
<i>unreasonable violence funny.</i>

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:42.340
Okay, let's forget about him.
You, the four-eyed geek.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:44.300
<i>Oh, well. He picked me. I have no choice.</i>

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.220
A: SAVE - B: NOT SAVE

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.140
The first question.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.390
There's a girl being attacked by a monster
in a cave. Will you save her, or...

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:50.140
Hey! Where the hell are you going?

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:52.100
A real hero never escapes.
Wait, right there!

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.270
What is this? Another world?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.780
Am I summoned as a legendary hero?

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.280
This is great! Wait, where has he gone?

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.700
<i>-The first question.</i>
-What?

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:03.280
<i>There's a girl being attacked by a monster</i>
<i>in a cave.</i>

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.950
<i>A: Save her. B: Do not save her.</i>

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.700
What's going on? Where am I?

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.200
-Hinoki!
<i>-Show me your answer.</i>

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.450
Mr. Haganeno...

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.960
DO SOMETHING WITH THIS

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.000
<i>Everything will be fine</i>
<i>if I could get to the church.</i>

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:14.960
<i>Wrong answer.</i>

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:16.460
Four-eyes geek!

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.960
<i>How could you ruin our 5th anniversary?</i>

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.630
Where the hell are we?

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:21.720
<i>It's so appropriate for you, isn't it?</i>

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:24.760
<i>You're not supposed to be there.</i>
<i>Stay here and enjoy leveling up.</i>

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.970
<i>-Bye.</i>
-Wait!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.510
-Seriously?
<i>-The hero Haganeno</i>

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:32.520
<i>has finally left for adventure. Nobody</i>
<i>knows if he could become a real hero...</i>

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.940
<i>Let's head to the town anyways.</i>

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:37.610
<i>...but it's certain that peace was</i>
<i>restored to the world after he'd left.</i>

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:40.940
-I want to appear, too!
-You're the last person they'd ask.

00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:10.620
Subtitle translation by Kanako Murakoshi
